msgstr "Changing an output's codec today is a configuration change, not a live switch: stored edits take effect by exporting the config and restarting the engine (the API marks these resources <0>apply: restart</0>). The codec token is also only lightly checked at present — if the build cannot encode the requested codec, the pipeline logs a warning and falls back to MPEG-2 rather than failing the run. So choose a codec your build and transport are known to carry (classic RTMP, for example, carries H.264 only), and verify the output really uses it — for example with <1>ffprobe</1>."

