#: src/pages/docs/concepts/ResiliencePage.tsx:102
msgid "Source connections are supervised. A stalled read times out rather than hanging forever; the supervisor then reconnects with exponential backoff (so a dead camera is not hammered) and keeps trying indefinitely, with the aim of recovering without operator action when the far end becomes usable again. Mid-stream surprises that normally break players, like a camera changing resolution or a stream resetting its timestamps, are absorbed inside the tile: the decoder re-initializes behind the frame store while the compositor keeps drawing the last good frame."
msgstr "Source connections are supervised. A stalled read times out rather than hanging forever; the supervisor then reconnects with exponential backoff (so a dead camera is not hammered) and keeps trying indefinitely, with the aim of recovering without operator action when the far end becomes usable again. Mid-stream surprises that normally break players, like a camera changing resolution or a stream resetting its timestamps, are absorbed inside the tile: the decoder re-initializes behind the frame store while the compositor keeps drawing the last good frame."

